cts|Images from Wiki Loves Monuments missing SDC location of creation|Taken with Nokia 5233", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "Nilakantha Palace:\nNilkantha is a charming spot named after an old shiva shrine which once exited here. The structure ,built of red stone, is a pleasure-house constructed by a governor of the mugal emporer Akbar in the sixteenth century, as recorded in an inscription on the site. This building has no architectural pretensions but its style is typical of the period of Akbar.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "Taken on\u00a09 September 2012, 16:10:14", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Anurodhraghuwanshi&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Anurodhraghuwanshi (page does not exist)\">Anurodhraghuwanshi</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 3.0", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "true", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "LicenseUrl": {"value": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "True", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "cc-by-sa-3.0", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}, "mime": "image/jpeg"}]}, "-5": {"ns": 6, "title": "File:Nilkanth Mahadev Temple Bhinmal Rajasthan India.jpg", "missing": "", "known": "", "imagerepository": "shared", "imageinfo": [{"size": 3036547, "width": 2448, "height": 3264, "thumburl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg/1920px-Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "thumbwidth": 1600, "thumbheight": 2133, "responsiveUrls": {"2": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ed/Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}, "thumbattribs": {"src": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg/1920px-Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "decoding": "async", "loading": "lazy", "width": 1600, "height": 2133, "srcset": "//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ed/Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"}, "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ed/Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nilkanth_Mahadev_Temple_Bhinmal_Rajasthan_India.jpg", "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=193935812", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2026-06-15 12:11:54", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "Nilkanth Mahadev Temple Bhinmal Rajasthan India", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Hindu temples in Rajasthan|Self-published work", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "Neelkanth Mahadev Temple, Bhinmal Located in the historic town of Bhinmal, in Rajasthan\u2019s Jalore district, the Neelkanth Mahadev Temple is a divine and grand Shiva temple. It is not only a center for spiritual practice but also a prominent religious tourist destination. Dedicated to Lord Shiva in his Neelkanth form, the temple offers a unique blend of devotion, faith, and inner peace for its devotees. \ud83d\uded5 Temple Highlights Majestic spire and intricately carved stone architecture Clean and peaceful surroundings, ideal for meditation and worship Daily evening Aarti offers a spiritually uplifting experience for visitors \ud83c\udf89 Major Festivals and Events Pran Pratishtha Festival: Held in January (17\u201327), featuring Kalash Yatra, Ram Katha, Yajna, and idol consecration rituals The event was graced by Uttarakhand Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami \ud83c\udfe8 Nearby Facilities Ample parking space near the temple Proper arrangements for prasad distribution, drinking water, and cleanliness Shops outside the temple offer easy access to puja materials Nearby guesthouses and hotels are available at affordable rates \ud83d\udcf8 Tourist Attractions Stunning sunset views from the temple premises The majestic Shiva flagpole (Dhwaja Stambh) at the entrance is a striking sight The nearby Amrit Kund (sacred water reservoir) holds deep religious significance \ud83e\uddfe Conclusion Neelkanth Mahadev Temple is not just a center for Shiva devotion, but also a place of serenity, cultural festivities, and spiritual power. If you\u2019re planning a visit to Bhinmal, make this temple a top priority\u2014it will leave you with a profound and peaceful experience.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "2026-05-29 12:30:14", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Mahaveer_Car_Accessories&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Mahaveer Car Accessories (page does not exist)\">Mahaveer Car Accessories</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "true", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "LicenseUrl": {"value": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "True", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "cc-by-sa-4.0", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}, "mime": "image/jpeg"}]}}}}